 const SECTIONS=[
-{"name":"Speed — the perf pass","where":"Deployed app","items":[["PF-3","FAILED 05/08 — readonly gate (retest after diagnosis)","hello@ (readonly) could create tours/artists. Code path IS guarded (requireWrite on /api/tours + /api/artists; readonly → 403). FIRST CHECK the account's actual role — Supabase SQL: select role, status from workspace_members wm join profiles p on p.id=wm.user_id where p.email='hello@...'; If role is not 'readonly', that's the whole bug — fix the row and retest. If it IS readonly and creation still succeeds, capture the request URL from devtools Network and report it."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — phase A (migration 256 CONFIRMED live in prod)","where":"Migration already pasted — Cowork verified the attachments table + lineage columns directly","items":[["RD-4","Saturday differs","Attach a different version to one show (routing_id): that show's advance packet lists the Saturday version; other shows keep the tour default."],["RD-5","Edits hit everywhere","Edit rows on an attached version: every place it's attached shows the change; other versions untouched."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — B1 · version/attach controls (tour surfaces)","where":"/operations/[tourId]/channel-list and /operations/[tourId]/stage-plot","items":[["VC-1","Version picker shows the family","Channel-list surface: the Version select lists the original (marked '(original)') + every saved version of the shown document."],["VC-2","Picking a version ATTACHES it","Select a different version: toast 'Tour channel list switched', page re-resolves to that version's rows, and Detach appears. This is the design — the picker answers 'which version is this tour using'."],["VC-3","Save as version… doesn't switch","Name one inline (Enter saves, Escape cancels): toast, new entry in the picker, but the tour STAYS on the current version — you attach it where it belongs yourself."],["VC-4","Attach to show… overrides one show only","Pick a routing row: toast names the city/date. That show's advance packet lists this version; the tour default and other shows are untouched."],["VC-5","Detach is honest","A tour resolving via the LEGACY scan shows no Detach. An attached tour shows it; detaching toasts and falls back to the legacy scan. Detach must never appear for a document the surface isn't actually showing."],["VC-6","Stage plot has the same row","Above the open plot editor (immediately on a 1-plot tour): same Version / Save as version / Attach to show / Detach controls; Detach only when the OPEN plot is the tour-attached one."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — B1 · the rider's tech section","where":"Rider editor on a RIDER pack that has a channel_list section","items":[["RS-1","Owned legacy section is read-only + Convert","The embedded channel list renders as a read-only sheet with the 'lives INSIDE the rider (legacy)' banner and a Convert button — no editable grid, no edit link."],["RS-2","Convert works end-to-end","Click Convert: toast, the section flips to 'Attached document' with a preview + 'Edit channel list ↗'. The new standalone doc exists (with every row copied), the original rows are still in the DB, and the doc is its own family root (no version label)."],["RS-3","Attached mode: Change… / Detach / Edit ↗","Change… lists channel-list documents on the tour + artist scope; picking one replaces the attachment. Edit ↗ opens the standalone editor (full grid). Detach returns to the legacy state."],["RS-4","Inherited sections untouched","An artist-inherited channel list still shows the tested override wall/flow — Convert is NOT offered there (its rows live on the parent pack; API refuses with a message saying to convert at the owning scope)."],["RS-5","Standalone channel-list docs unaffected","Opening a channel_list PACK (from /rider-packs or Edit ↗) still gives the FULL editor — grid, dropdowns, stage boxes, patch grid."]]},{"name":"Rider builder — B2 · fixed groups","where":"/rider-packs/[id]?mode=edit on a plain rider pack","items":[["GB-1","Four fixed tabs, legacy lands in Production","Production · Technical · Hospitality · Travel tabs with section counts; every pre-existing section sits under Production; the old accordion + left template library + drop zone are gone."],["GB-2","Rail selects, canvas shows ONE section","The left rail lists the active group's sections; clicking one puts it on the canvas, open, no collapse chevron. Fields edit exactly as before (add, drag-reorder, delete)."],["GB-3","Add section is group-aware","In Technical the menu offers Audio/FOH, Monitors/IEMs, Lighting, Backline, Risers/Stage (+ Blank); in Production, Contacts + Schedule. A section added from a tab STAYS in that tab after a reload."],["GB-4","+ Add group is curated only","The menu offers exactly Security, Merch, Press & Promo, Parking & Access, Catering, Local Crew — no freeform input anywhere. Adding one opens its tab; templates for it (e.g. Security) appear in ITS add menu."],["GB-5","Move to group persists","The select in the section card header moves the section; tab counts update; the move survives a hard reload (metadata.group)."],["GB-6","Rail drag reorders within the group","Drag a rail row above another: order changes, persists on reload, and sections in OTHER groups keep their relative order."],["GB-7","Properties rail still wired","Click a field on the canvas: the right panel opens; editing label/type updates the field; delete from the panel removes it."],["GB-8","Empty added group is session-local","Add a group, put nothing in it, reload: the tab is gone (by design — it returns when a section lands in it). No error."]]},{"name":"Venue read view — B3 · grouped","where":"/r/[token] (rider web link) — needs a pack whose sections span ≥2 groups","items":[["RV-1","Single-group packs unchanged","A legacy all-Production rider's public page looks exactly as before: no group chips, no left list, same flat flow."],["RV-2","Multi-group packs get the nav","Move a section to Technical in the builder, reopen the web link: sticky group chips up top + a left section list (desktop), group headings in the body; chips + list scroll-to the right anchors."],["RV-3","Print stays a linear document","Print preview (or the PDF): no chips, no side list — cover, TOC, then sections with group headings; page breaks sane."],["RV-4","PDF group headings","Download the rider PDF for the same multi-group pack: uppercase group headings above each group's sections; a single-group pack's PDF is unchanged."]]},{"name":"One show link — B4 ⚠ paste migration 257 first","where":"database/migrations/257_show_links.sql → then /advance/[tour]/[routing] packet page","items":[["SL-1","Migration 257 pastes clean","Runs without error; re-running is a no-op."],["SL-2","Copy show link mints once","Packet page → Public share → 'Copy show link': URL /s/[token] lands on the clipboard. Click it again: SAME URL (mint-or-reuse, no link mill)."],["SL-3","/s/[token] opens logged-out","Open in a private window: header shows artist · tour · date · venue/city (venue via the resolver, never raw routing columns) + the five tabs. No login bounce."],["SL-4","Advance tab embeds the intake form","With a live venue-intake link for the show: the form renders in-page + 'Open in its own tab ↗'. Without one: a plain 'not opened yet' message, not an error."],["SL-5","Rider + Channel list tabs read grouped","Rider tab renders the show's riders with the B3 grouped read view; Channel list tab shows the attached (or fallback) list's grid. Empty states name what's missing."],["SL-6","Stage plot renders inline","The attached (or newest tour) plot draws as SVG in the tab; no plot → a clean empty state."],["SL-7","Downloads: bundled PDF via the show token","The download button produces the packet PDF using the /s/ token (no packet link needed). Old /a/ packet links still download fine."],["SL-8","Old doors still open","Existing /r/, /a/, /advance-intake/, /share/advance links all still work; /settings and /signup still bounce to login (the /s/ prefix swallowed nothing)."]]},{"name":"Walk-feedback fixes — 2026-08-06 ⚠ paste 258+259+260 for the template items","where":"Rider editor · tour channel-list · artist page","items":[["WF-1","Builder reads as a builder","Group tabs are big with a hard orange underline; the section rail is a real panel; the active section is unmistakable. Not subtle."],["WF-2","Riders delete from the editor","The editor header has Delete (confirm → back to the tour riders list / artist page). Lists still delete as before."],["WF-3","Show view is grouped","A rider spanning ≥2 groups shows group chips + headings in Show mode, same grammar as the builder. One-group riders: plain scroll, unchanged."],["WF-4","Channel list edits without overriding","On /operations/[tour]/channel-list an INHERITED list shows the rows read-only + one button: 'Create this tour's editable copy'. Click it: the tour gets its own attached document, fully editable, artist master untouched. No override bounce."],["WF-5","Tour picker is one honest list","Artist page: 'TOURS · N' header + New tour; every tour always listed (upcoming asc, PAST group below); visible Operations · Budget · Advance links per row; the previously-opened tour is highlighted, never hides the list."],["WF-6","Templates are deep (paste 258/259/260 first)","Rider 'Add section' menus offer 17 enriched/new templates with 12-25 fields; the advance library carries the full 17-section / ~427-field catalog; budget template gains the missing income/cost/percentage lines. Re-pasting any of the three is a no-op."]]},{"name":"Payroll — the canonical flat-seven (⚠ needs the payroll+income patch + migration 261)","where":"/operations/[tourId]/payroll","items":[["PAY-1","One flat rates grid","Columns: Flat day · Flat tour · Show · Travel · Rehearsal · Press/Radio · Per diem · Advance — all editable for everyone. NO Rate type column, NO '+ Add rate type'/'Manage' buttons. Zero amounts render blank, not $0.00."],["PAY-2","Editing is instant","Type a rate, Enter: the cursor drops to the next row IMMEDIATELY — no wait, no reclick. Tab moves right. A failed save toasts + reverts the cell."],["PAY-3","The math agrees","Pick a person with painted + unpainted days: the Rates grid's Days / Total fee / Total PD equal that person's matrix row totals exactly (tour-default days now count everywhere). No more US$0 against a full matrix."],["PAY-4","Stacking warns, still bills","Give one person BOTH a Flat day and a Show rate: a ⚠ appears by their name (hover explains); the total = flat day × worked days + show × show days (sum, not either/or)."],["PAY-5","The full brush palette","Brushes: Tour default · Show · Rehearsal · Travel · Promo/Radio · Off · PD · No tour. Off paints an O tile (bills the TRAVEL rate + PD). PD paints a grey PD tile (per diem only, no fee). No tour empties the cell (nothing)."],["PAY-6","Per diem = every assigned day","Per diem counts Show/Travel/Rehearsal/Promo/Off/PD days; a No-tour day earns nothing. Paint a PD day: Total PD ticks up, Total fee doesn't."],["PAY-7","Press/Radio fallback","A Promo/Radio day bills the SHOW rate while the person's Press/Radio cell is empty; enter a Press/Radio amount and the promo day bills that instead."],["PAY-8","Retired types stopped billing","Weekly + custom columns (e.g. 'Show Day') are gone from the grid and no longer bill — Dillon's $200 must be re-entered in the real Show column. Amounts survive in the DB (reversible), they just don't count."],["PAY-9","Budget salary agrees","After a rate/day edit, the Budget Salary + Per-Diem lines for that person match the payroll totals (the reconcile now counts effective days too)."]]},{"name":"Income — the lean sheet + deal slide-over (⚠ same patch)","where":"/budget/[tourId] → Income tab","items":[["INC-1","One sheet, no toggle","The Projected/Actual toggle is GONE. Columns: Date · Type · Venue · City · Deal summary · Contracted · Settled · Variance. Settled + Variance are blank until a show settles."],["INC-2","Row opens the deal slide-over","Open a row: orange hero (date·city eyebrow, venue headline, status chip), then a Contracted | Settled | Variance KPI band. The grid's old generic row panel does NOT also open."],["INC-3","Deal edits save on blur","Change the guarantee in the slide-over, blur: Contracted moves in the ledger AND in the grid behind it. On a locked version, a proposed edit raises the version modal, not a silent fail."],["INC-4","The waterfall ledger","'Contracted — the maths' reads Guarantee → − withholding → + Overage ƒ → + Merch ƒ → + VIP ƒ → CONTRACTED, mono right-aligned. Click ƒ on a line → it becomes an editable override (OVERRIDE tag); Revert recomputes from the inputs."],["INC-5","Settled is walk-only","No settled figure is typeable in the grid. A settled show carries the green AUTO · SETTLEMENT chip; the slide-over's Settled card shows the settled ledger + a green 'Open the settlement walk →' button that lands on the settlement page."],["INC-6","Manual override is explicit","'Manual override…' opens the amber panel; entering a figure flips the chip to MANUAL. That's the ONLY manual path — no ambient actual-cell typing anywhere."],["INC-7","FX strip survives","A tour with foreign-currency shows still gets the FX strip (live = red count, locked-at-settlement = blue count) above the sheet."]]},{"name":"Rider fixes — rename · menu · layout (batch 5c)","where":"Any rider builder","items":[["RB-1","Rider renames from the title","Click the rider title in the builder hero (pencil shows): input in place, Enter/blur saves, name updates everywhere. Empty input keeps the old name."],["RB-2","Save failures speak","Force a failing edit (e.g. edit while logged out in another tab): a toast names the server error — not just the tiny save chip."],["RB-3","Add-section menu floats free","At the bottom of a long section rail, open Add section: the menu overlays (portal), never clipped by the rail; flips above when the viewport below is tight."],["RB-4","Fields flow 2-up","A section with many compact fields lays them out side by side on a wide canvas instead of one giant stack."]]},{"name":"Channel list — created where it lives","where":"/operations/[tourId]/channel-list","items":[["CL-1","Create button on the page","With no channel list: a New channel list button (plus a compact header action when one exists). No detour through Riders."],["CL-2","Tour-wide + honest banner","Creating it shows: 'Assigned to every show on this tour — it will appear in the tour's rider automatically.' The list is immediately editable; the tour's rider shows it."]]},{"name":"Rider catalog — artist demands (⚠ paste 263; do NOT re-paste 258 after)","where":"Rider builder → Add section","items":[["CAT-1","Rider-centric templates","Menus offer Hospitality Rider, Dressing Rooms, Catering/Buyout, Backline, Audio/PA, Lighting, Security & Barricade, Merch, Parking & Access, Towels & Laundry, Bus Stock, Guest List & Passes. 'Production & Amenities / Wi-Fi available' is gone (now Production Office)."],["CAT-2","Content reads as demands","Open Hospitality Rider: still/sparkling water, local beer, fresh fruit, towels count etc — artist asks, not venue answers. Your own custom templates untouched."]]},{"name":"Native controls — killed site-wide","where":"Anywhere","items":[["UI-1","No white checkboxes","Every checkbox/radio renders orange-accented and theme-correct (payroll catch-up, rider field lists, batch panels)."],["UI-2","Selects match the app","Dropdowns show token colors + custom chevron (no OS grey arrow); select POPUPS render dark in dark mode (color-scheme). Light mode unaffected."]]},{"name":"Settlement — the full process (⚠ paste 262 first)","where":"/budget/[tourId]/settlement","items":[["SET-1","KPI strip + rail","Outstanding · Settled · Not settled · Awaiting payment · Unsettled N of M up top; show cards carry SETTLED/DUE chips and status-hued rails."],["SET-2","Catch-up batch","With played-unsettled shows: the panel lists them with contracted guarantees; Select all; 'Settle N shows' runs sequentially with n/N progress; Full & Final toggle (default on). Each show's income cascades exactly like a manual settle."],["SET-3","Deal & box office card","Set Door deal 80%, tickets 1000, gross 40000: the waterfall renders Gross → BO fees → Net BO → expenses → Split pool → Artist share → Suggested overage."],["SET-4","Apply is the consent","Nothing writes until you click 'Apply … to Overage' — then reconciled_overage lands in the walk and the income row updates. Guarantee-only shows: quiet hint, numbers unchanged to the penny."],["SET-5","BO fees split honestly","Add a Facility fee deduction: it renders in the waterfall, NOT the guarantee-side Deductions group — but the income cascade total still includes it (check the income row's deductions)."]]},{"name":"Day view — the Tour Book standard","where":"/operations/[tourId]/day/[routingId]","items":[["DV-1","Hero + fact strip","Day-type-tinted hero: date·artist·tour eyebrow, city headline, venue subline, day-type chip, facts (N schedule · first call · hotel · N flights · Day P&L)."],["DV-2","Flights land on the day","A flight departing/arriving that date shows in the Flights card (mono times, JFK → ATL, passenger chips, conf). This NEVER worked before — flights were keyed to a field the grid doesn't set."],["DV-3","Files on the day","Show-scoped rider assets + routing-linked files render with open links. Driver/accountant slices don't see them."],["DV-4","Day sheet PDF, one click","The direct 'Day sheet PDF' button downloads: schedule, venue, contacts, lodging, flights+passengers, notes."],["DV-5","Crew view stays clean","View as crew/token link: money + notes still absent (not hidden — absent)."]]},{"name":"Rooming — the Unassigned Hotel flood ends","where":"/operations/[tourId]/rooming + /budget","items":[["RM-1","One honest line per hotel","Add a room on a date with no hotel: budget shows ONE line 'Hotel — {city} · {date} · N rooms' — not a pile of 'Unassigned Hotel' lines."],["RM-2","Placeholders reuse + heal","More rooms on the same date reuse the same placeholder; existing 'Unassigned Hotel' junk renames itself as you edit that date. Real hotels label as '{name} — {city} · {check-in} · N rooms'."],["RM-3","Nights tab is live","Paint a room in the grid, flip to Nights WITHOUT reloading: it's there (was: stale until hard refresh). Same-day placeholder counts as 1 night."]]}
+{"name":"Speed — the perf pass","where":"Deployed app","items":[["PF-3","FAILED 05/08 — readonly gate (retest after diagnosis)","hello@ (readonly) could create tours/artists. Code path IS guarded (requireWrite on /api/tours + /api/artists; readonly → 403). FIRST CHECK the account's actual role — Supabase SQL: select role, status from workspace_members wm join profiles p on p.id=wm.user_id where p.email='hello@...'; If role is not 'readonly', that's the whole bug — fix the row and retest. If it IS readonly and creation still succeeds, capture the request URL from devtools Network and report it."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — phase A (migration 256 CONFIRMED live in prod)","where":"Migration already pasted — Cowork verified the attachments table + lineage columns directly","items":[["RD-4","Saturday differs","Attach a different version to one show (routing_id): that show's advance packet lists the Saturday version; other shows keep the tour default."],["RD-5","Edits hit everywhere","Edit rows on an attached version: every place it's attached shows the change; other versions untouched."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — B1 · version/attach controls (tour surfaces)","where":"/operations/[tourId]/channel-list and /operations/[tourId]/stage-plot","items":[["VC-1","Version picker shows the family","Channel-list surface: the Version select lists the original (marked '(original)') + every saved version of the shown document."],["VC-2","Picking a version ATTACHES it","Select a different version: toast 'Tour channel list switched', page re-resolves to that version's rows, and Detach appears. This is the design — the picker answers 'which version is this tour using'."],["VC-3","Save as version… doesn't switch","Name one inline (Enter saves, Escape cancels): toast, new entry in the picker, but the tour STAYS on the current version — you attach it where it belongs yourself."],["VC-4","Attach to show… overrides one show only","Pick a routing row: toast names the city/date. That show's advance packet lists this version; the tour default and other shows are untouched."],["VC-5","Detach is honest","A tour resolving via the LEGACY scan shows no Detach. An attached tour shows it; detaching toasts and falls back to the legacy scan. Detach must never appear for a document the surface isn't actually showing."],["VC-6","Stage plot has the same row","Above the open plot editor (immediately on a 1-plot tour): same Version / Save as version / Attach to show / Detach controls; Detach only when the OPEN plot is the tour-attached one."]]},{"name":"Rider decouple — B1 · the rider's tech section","where":"Rider editor on a RIDER pack that has a channel_list section","items":[["RS-1","Owned legacy section is read-only + Convert","The embedded channel list renders as a read-only sheet with the 'lives INSIDE the rider (legacy)' banner and a Convert button — no editable grid, no edit link."],["RS-2","Convert works end-to-end","Click Convert: toast, the section flips to 'Attached document' with a preview + 'Edit channel list ↗'. The new standalone doc exists (with every row copied), the original rows are still in the DB, and the doc is its own family root (no version label)."],["RS-3","Attached mode: Change… / Detach / Edit ↗","Change… lists channel-list documents on the tour + artist scope; picking one replaces the attachment. Edit ↗ opens the standalone editor (full grid). Detach returns to the legacy state."],["RS-4","Inherited sections untouched","An artist-inherited channel list still shows the tested override wall/flow — Convert is NOT offered there (its rows live on the parent pack; API refuses with a message saying to convert at the owning scope)."],["RS-5","Standalone channel-list docs unaffected","Opening a channel_list PACK (from /rider-packs or Edit ↗) still gives the FULL editor — grid, dropdowns, stage boxes, patch grid."]]},{"name":"Rider builder — B2 · fixed groups","where":"/rider-packs/[id]?mode=edit on a plain rider pack","items":[["GB-1","Four fixed tabs, legacy lands in Production","Production · Technical · Hospitality · Travel tabs with section counts; every pre-existing section sits under Production; the old accordion + left template library + drop zone are gone."],["GB-2","Rail selects, canvas shows ONE section","The left rail lists the active group's sections; clicking one puts it on the canvas, open, no collapse chevron. Fields edit exactly as before (add, drag-reorder, delete)."],["GB-3","Add section is group-aware","In Technical the menu offers Audio/FOH, Monitors/IEMs, Lighting, Backline, Risers/Stage (+ Blank); in Production, Contacts + Schedule. A section added from a tab STAYS in that tab after a reload."],["GB-4","+ Add group is curated only","The menu offers exactly Security, Merch, Press & Promo, Parking & Access, Catering, Local Crew — no freeform input anywhere. Adding one opens its tab; templates for it (e.g. Security) appear in ITS add menu."],["GB-5","Move to group persists","The select in the section card header moves the section; tab counts update; the move survives a hard reload (metadata.group)."],["GB-6","Rail drag reorders within the group","Drag a rail row above another: order changes, persists on reload, and sections in OTHER groups keep their relative order."],["GB-7","Properties rail still wired","Click a field on the canvas: the right panel opens; editing label/type updates the field; delete from the panel removes it."],["GB-8","Empty added group is session-local","Add a group, put nothing in it, reload: the tab is gone (by design — it returns when a section lands in it). No error."]]},{"name":"Venue read view — B3 · grouped","where":"/r/[token] (rider web link) — needs a pack whose sections span ≥2 groups","items":[["RV-1","Single-group packs unchanged","A legacy all-Production rider's public page looks exactly as before: no group chips, no left list, same flat flow."],["RV-2","Multi-group packs get the nav","Move a section to Technical in the builder, reopen the web link: sticky group chips up top + a left section list (desktop), group headings in the body; chips + list scroll-to the right anchors."],["RV-3","Print stays a linear document","Print preview (or the PDF): no chips, no side list — cover, TOC, then sections with group headings; page breaks sane."],["RV-4","PDF group headings","Download the rider PDF for the same multi-group pack: uppercase group headings above each group's sections; a single-group pack's PDF is unchanged."]]},{"name":"One show link — B4 ⚠ paste migration 257 first","where":"database/migrations/257_show_links.sql → then /advance/[tour]/[routing] packet page","items":[["SL-1","Migration 257 pastes clean","Runs without error; re-running is a no-op."],["SL-2","Copy show link mints once","Packet page → Public share → 'Copy show link': URL /s/[token] lands on the clipboard. Click it again: SAME URL (mint-or-reuse, no link mill)."],["SL-3","/s/[token] opens logged-out","Open in a private window: header shows artist · tour · date · venue/city (venue via the resolver, never raw routing columns) + the five tabs. No login bounce."],["SL-4","Advance tab embeds the intake form","With a live venue-intake link for the show: the form renders in-page + 'Open in its own tab ↗'. Without one: a plain 'not opened yet' message, not an error."],["SL-5","Rider + Channel list tabs read grouped","Rider tab renders the show's riders with the B3 grouped read view; Channel list tab shows the attached (or fallback) list's grid. Empty states name what's missing."],["SL-6","Stage plot renders inline","The attached (or newest tour) plot draws as SVG in the tab; no plot → a clean empty state."],["SL-7","Downloads: bundled PDF via the show token","The download button produces the packet PDF using the /s/ token (no packet link needed). Old /a/ packet links still download fine."],["SL-8","Old doors still open","Existing /r/, /a/, /advance-intake/, /share/advance links all still work; /settings and /signup still bounce to login (the /s/ prefix swa